def reachable_cycle_regions(request):
    "Accept the public request and return a dict with regions and reachable. regions is a list of strongly connected vertex groups that contain at least one directed cycle. Each group is a dict with a stations list and a transitions list containing all original edges internal to that group. reachable maps every station ID to a list of indices of the listed groups it can reach. Include one-vertex self-loop groups and preserve parallel transition rows.\n\nLocal check: Use P, A, B, C, and D, with P reaching A and C through A or directly, A and B mutually reachable, C having only a self-loop, and D isolated. Assert that regions have exactly the member sets {'A', 'B'} and {'C'}. P and A can reach both regions, C can reach only its own, and D reaches none. Values may use either region index order."
    raise NotImplementedError

def maximum_cycle_mean(region):
    'Accept a cycle-containing strongly connected region with stations and internal transitions. Return a two-integer list [numerator, denominator] with positive denominator representing the exact greatest mean gain over any nonempty directed cycle in that region. Preserve negative means, independent parallel edges, and single-edge loops.\n\nLocal check: Pass stations A and B and gains -5 on A to B, -2 on a parallel A to B edge, -3 on B to A, and -6 on A to A. Assert the result is the fraction -5/2. The parallel edge and negative feasible result both affect this check.'
    raise NotImplementedError

